# Byte-exact evidence fixtures: never let git translate line endings.
#
# Git's binary autodetection only scans the FIRST 8000 BYTES for a NUL, so a
# compressed image whose first NUL falls past that window is classified as text
# and has its LF bytes rewritten to CRLF on checkout. `core.autocrlf` defaults
# to true on GitHub's windows-latest runners, which is how a fixture-backed test
# fails on Windows only, while the code is provably correct.
tests/data/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
